@startuml M6-Data-Flow

' Data flow through complete search pipeline: Input -> Crawl -> Index -> Search -> Output
' Shows how data transforms at each stage: seeds become documents, documents become inverted index, queries become ranked results
' Three MapReduce jobs run in parallel during indexing: extract terms, calculate TF-IDF stats, compute PageRank
' Each stage persists intermediate results in storage (CRAWL_STORE, INDEX_STORE)

!define BGCOLOR #F5F5F5
skinparam backgroundColor BGCOLOR
skinparam componentFontColor #333
skinparam ArrowColor #333
skinparam packageBorderColor #666
skinparam shadowing false

title M6 Search Engine - Data Flow (Crawl -> Index -> Search)

rectangle "INPUT PHASE" as INPUT {
  database "Seed File\n(owner/repo)" as SEEDS
  component "Seed Loader" as LOADER
}

rectangle "CRAWL PHASE" as CRAWL_PH {
  component "Frontier\nQueue" as FRONTIER
  component "GitHub\nAPI" as GH_API
  component "README\nDownloader" as DOWNLOADER
  database "Crawled Docs\n{docId: content}" as CRAWL_STORE
}

rectangle "INDEX PHASE" as INDEX_PH {
  
  rectangle "MapReduce Job 1: Terms" as MR1 {
    component "Extract\nText" as MR1_MAP
    component "Normalize\n& Stem" as MR1_SHUF
    component "Group by\nTerm" as MR1_RED
  }
  
  rectangle "MapReduce Job 2: Stats" as MR2 {
    component "Count\nOccurrences" as MR2_MAP
    component "Aggregate\nby Term" as MR2_SHUF
    component "Calculate\nTF/DF" as MR2_RED
  }
  
  rectangle "MapReduce Job 3: PageRank" as MR3 {
    component "Extract\nLinks" as MR3_MAP
    component "Distribute\nPR" as MR3_RED
  }
  
  database "Index Storage" as INDEX_STORE {
    artifact "Inverted Index\n{term: [docIds]}" as INV_IDX
    artifact "TF Stats\n{term: {doc: freq}}" as TF_STATS
    artifact "DF Stats\n{term: count}" as DF_STATS
    artifact "PageRank\n{doc: score}" as PR_SCORES
  }
}

rectangle "SEARCH PHASE" as SEARCH_PH {
  component "Parse\nQuery" as Q_PARSE
  component "Process\nQuery" as Q_PROC
  component "Lookup\nPostings" as Q_LOOKUP
  component "Calculate\nScores" as Q_SCORE
  component "Rank\nResults" as Q_RANK
  component "Format\nResults" as Q_FMT
}

artifact "TF-IDF" as TFIDF
artifact "Metadata\nBoost" as BOOST

rectangle "OUTPUT" as OUTPUT {
  component "Display\nResults" as DISPLAY
}

' Input Flow
SEEDS --> LOADER : load repos
LOADER --> FRONTIER : initialize queue

' Crawl Flow
FRONTIER --> DOWNLOADER : next repo
DOWNLOADER --> GH_API : fetch
GH_API --> DOWNLOADER : README content
DOWNLOADER --> CRAWL_STORE : store doc
DOWNLOADER --> FRONTIER : mark done

' Index Flow
CRAWL_STORE --> MR1_MAP : read all docs
MR1_MAP --> MR1_SHUF : tokenize
MR1_SHUF --> MR1_RED : collect terms
MR1_RED --> INV_IDX : store posting lists

CRAWL_STORE --> MR2_MAP : count terms
MR2_MAP --> MR2_SHUF : accumulate
MR2_SHUF --> MR2_RED : calculate stats
MR2_RED --> TF_STATS : store TF
MR2_RED --> DF_STATS : store DF

CRAWL_STORE --> MR3_MAP : extract links
MR3_MAP --> MR3_RED : iterative PR
MR3_RED --> PR_SCORES : store scores

' Search Flow
Q_PARSE --> Q_PROC : "javascript framework"
Q_PROC --> Q_LOOKUP : stem + tokens
Q_LOOKUP --> INV_IDX : lookup postings
INV_IDX --> Q_SCORE : candidate docs

Q_SCORE --> TF_STATS : fetch TF
Q_SCORE --> DF_STATS : fetch DF
TF_STATS --> TFIDF : calculate
DF_STATS --> TFIDF : calculate
Q_SCORE --> BOOST : boost by metadata

TFIDF --> Q_RANK : TF-IDF scores
BOOST --> Q_RANK : metadata scores
Q_RANK --> Q_FMT : top K results
Q_FMT --> DISPLAY : formatted

note right of CRAWL_PH
  **Input:** Seed list (e.g., nodejs/node)
  **Process:** Download README files
  **Output:** Raw document text + metadata
  **Persistence:** Frontier state, seen repos
end note

note right of INDEX_PH
  **Input:** All crawled documents
  **Process:** Three MapReduce jobs
    1. Extract & normalize terms
    2. Calculate TF-IDF statistics
    3. Compute PageRank iteratively
  **Output:** Inverted index + scoring data
  **Storage:** All data persisted in KV store
end note

note right of SEARCH_PH
  **Input:** User query "javascript framework"
  **Process:** 
    1. Parse query terms
    2. Lookup inverted index
    3. Fetch TF/DF/PageRank
    4. Calculate final scores
    5. Rank by relevance
  **Output:** Ranked results (top 10)
end note

@enduml
